  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array A=A1,A2,…,ANA = A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA=A1​,A2​,…,AN​ of size NNN.\n\nConsider a subsequence S=S1,S2,…,SMS = S_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_MS=S1​,S2​,…,SM​ of AAA. Let us define the Goodness of subsequence SSS as follows:\n\n\n\nSort the subsequence SSS in non-decreasing order.\n\n\n\n\nThen, the Goodness of subsequence SSS is the number of indices such that Si=i,S_i = i,Si​=i, where\n(1≤i≤∣S∣).(1 \\le i \\le |S|).(1≤i≤∣S∣).\n\n\n\nFor example, suppose A=[10,3,2,5,11,3,1,12]A = [ 10, 3, 2, 5, 11, 3, 1, 12 ]A=[10,3,2,5,11,3,1,12], and the subsequence is S=[3,2,5,3,1]S = [ 3, 2, 5, 3, 1 ]S=[3,2,5,3,1]. After sorting, S=[1,2,3,3,5]S = [ 1, 2, 3, 3, 5 ]S=[1,2,3,3,5], and so the Goodness  of SSS is 444.\n\nConsider all the 2N−12^N - 12N−1 possible non-empty subsequences of array AAA, and find the sum of all their Goodness.\n\nSince the answer can be large, output the answer modulo 109+7.10^9 + 7.109+7.\n\n**Note:** A sequence SSS is a subsequence of array AAA if SSS can be obtained from AAA by deletion of several (possibly, zero) elements. For example, [3,1][3,1][3,1] is a subsequence of [3,2,1][3,2,1][3,2,1] and [4,3,1][4,3,1][4,3,1], but not a subsequence of [1,3,3,7][1,3,3,7][1,3,3,7] and [3,10,4][3,10,4][3,10,4].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN - the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers, A1,A2,A3,...,AN.A_1, A_2, A_3,..., A_N.A1​,A2​,A3​,...,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the answer modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\leq A_i \\leq N 1≤Ai​≤N for each 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
