        "input": "4\n2\n1 2\n5\n3 2 5 5 3\n4\n1 1 2 1\n6\n6 4 5 2 3 1",
        "output": "3\n5\n17\n63",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTestcase 1: The given array is [1,2][1, 2][1,2]. There are 3 possible non-empty subsequences:\n\n[1][1][1]. The Goodness of this subsequence is 111, since S1=1S_1 = 1S1​=1.\n[2][2][2]. The Goodness of this subsequence is 000.\n[1,2][1, 2][1,2]. The Goodness of this subsequence is 222, since S1=1S_1 = 1S1​=1 and S2=2S_2 = 2S2​=2.\n\nThus the total sum is 1+0+2=31 + 0 + 2 = 31+0+2=3, which is the answer."
      }
